The priority ladder is the institutional margin that decides who bears a shortfall. Two ladders are compared at two reporting lags, twenty seeds per cell: one that serves consumption before production, and one that serves production before consumption. The aggregate is close to unchanged across the two, which is Corollary 3 stated as a fact about the model, while output, plan fulfilment and the recovery half-life diverge sharply. Generated by `scripts/paper_tables.py` from `results/`. Source: `reference_results/`.
